  "models": {
    "trace": "Nearest live Leak Source through the shared flying cursor; target-free and graphic-hidden source markers do not block selection. Native selector and aura both use radius.25 plus source body radius.1. Existing original-route progress is suspended during tracing.",
    "contact": "One tracked aura parent per source deployment, removed on departure, source invalidation or ability retirement. Each accepted parent creates a derived flag on the Bag with that Leak Source as its special source. Default single-flag replacement follows stable spawn order for simultaneous entries; retiring an older parent cannot remove its replacement flag. Overlapping Bags retain separate source-owned parents.",
    "feeding": "AtkUp requires a source in contact and an accepted flag, gates new casts under silence, honors action interruption, and holds movement for anim_duration11. Its accepted non-silenceable10.5-second parent keeps pulsing under later silence, each second after the first interval. A pulse without the flag interrupts the skill without resetting its cooldown. Stacks are independent permanent ATK MULTIPLIER contributions using skill atk.07 and max_stack_cnt40. The15-second skill cooldown starts on accepted cast and runs in real time, retaining its remaining amount after interruption, following the shared enemy skill scheduler.",
    "completion": "Only natural expiration of the feeding parent triggers the current flag back to its captured contact parent. That parent must still exist on the same live source deployment and its Bag must still be skill-affecting. It kills that parent owner, never a freshly selected nearest source. Retirement, interruption and early parent removal do not synthesize completion.",
    "passive": "The independent non-silenceable infinite AoeDamage parent pulses every canonical interval1 with current ATK and current selectable all-motion bodies within canonical range_radius1.6. Camouflage is bypassed by area selection; true hiding/untargetability and sleep are not. Owner control and the feeding clock do not pause its timer; hidden or retired deployments cannot emit output.",
    "limits": "Numeric callback/FSM dispatch, collider-edge contacts, same-tick contact replacement order, blackboard substitution, cooldown start and interruption timing use explicit shared-engine mappings. Native compiled/frame parity and visual size/effects remain unclaimed."
  }
